ADDUSER(8)                  System Manager's Manual                 ADDUSER(8)

NAME
       adduser, addgroup - add or manipulate users and groups

SYNOPSIS
       adduser [options] USER
       adduser --system [options] USER
       adduser --group GROUP
       addgroup [options] GROUP
       addgroup --system [options] GROUP
       adduser USER GROUP

DESCRIPTION
       adduser and addgroup add users and groups to the system.  They are
       friendlier front ends to the account databases /etc/passwd,
       /etc/shadow and /etc/group.  The program behaves as addgroup when it is
       invoked under that name.

       Five modes of operation are available:

       adduser USER
              Add a normal user.  A user id is allocated from the range
              FIRST_UID..LAST_UID (1000..59999).  Unless overridden, a group
              with the same name as the user is created (a usergroup) and used
              as the primary group.  A home directory is created under /home,
              seeded from /etc/skel, and owned by the new user.  Finally passwd
              is run to set the account's password.

       adduser --system USER
              Add a system user.  A user id is allocated from the system range
              (100..999), the login shell is /usr/sbin/nologin, the home
              directory defaults to /nonexistent and no password is set.

       adduser --group GROUP, addgroup GROUP
              Add a group.  A group id is allocated from FIRST_GID..LAST_GID.

       addgroup --system GROUP
              Add a group from the system range (100..999).

       adduser USER GROUP
              Add an existing user to an existing group.

OPTIONS
       --system              create a system account
       --group               create a group, or a usergroup with --system
       --uid ID              force the user id
       --gid ID              force the (primary) group id
       --ingroup GROUP       set the primary group by name (must exist)
       --home DIR            set the home directory
       --shell SHELL         set the login shell
       --comment TEXT        set the GECOS/comment field (also --gecos)
       --no-create-home      do not create the home directory
       --disabled-password   do not set a password
       --disabled-login      like --disabled-password and set a nologin shell
       --add-extra-groups    add the user to the configured extra groups
       --firstuid ID, --lastuid ID
                             override the user id range
       --firstgid ID, --lastgid ID
                             override the group id range
       --allow-all-names, --allow-bad-names
                             relax the user/group name check
       --quiet, --verbose, --debug
                             adjust the amount of output
       --conf FILE           configuration file (accepted, unused)
       --help                display this help
       --version             display version

       When --comment is not given for a normal user, adduser prompts
       interactively for the GECOS fields (Full Name, Room Number, Work Phone,
       Home Phone, Other) if standard input is a terminal.

FILES
       /etc/passwd   user account database
       /etc/shadow   encrypted passwords
       /etc/group    group database
       /etc/skel     skeleton files copied into new home directories

NOTES
       Only the superuser may add users or groups.  adduser and addgroup are
       the same program; the mode is chosen from the invocation name and the
       options.

SEE ALSO
       passwd(1), id(1), groups(1)

